				2515,
				78
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Add pub fn doc comments and normalize extension host references\n\nAdd `///` doc comments on every public notification atom function across all 40+ Server notification atoms, closing the gap between module-level docs and each individual handler. Each comment captures the wire method, its purpose, Sky event destination, and any idiosyncratic behaviour (channel draining, handle disambiguation, shape canonicalisation).\n\nAlso add doc comments on all Client public functions (CheckSideCarHealth, ConnectToSideCar, DisconnectFromSideCar, IsClientConnected, IsShuttingDown, MarkShutdown, PublishNotification, SendNotification, SendRequest, SubscribeNotifications, SubscriberCount, TryConnectSingle, WaitForClientConnection) and both Support helpers (RelayToSky, UnregisterByHandle).\n\nNormalise remaining inline references from \"Cocoon\" to \"Extension Host\" throughout doc comments and constants (DefaultCocoonAddress, DEFAULT_COCOON_PORT, RegisterCommand, TerminalLifecycle, UnregisterScmProvider). Update the multiplexer reference from OpenChannelFromCocoon to OpenChannelFromSidecar in Library.rs to match the LAND-PATCH identifier. Strip `Vine::` prefix from module-level headers in Client/mod.rs and Server/mod.rs for consistency with the rest of the crate.\n\nNo behavioural changes — documentation and reference consistency only.",
			"SHA": "e36bf0fc178fc9a626d758f6a449cbccfae36570"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:21:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2515,
				20
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Add comprehensive doc comments and normalize extension host references\n\nAdd module-level and item-level doc comments across every visible surface of the crate — Client (NotificationFrame, SendRequest, Shared, mod), Error (variant table, recoverability, tonic::Status mapping), Host, Library, Multiplexer, and all Server notification atoms (OutputAppend, OutputChannelClear, OutputChannelDispose, OutputChannelShow, OutputClear, OutputCreate, OutputDispose, OutputShow, ProgressComplete, Support).\n\nNormalise all inline references from \"Cocoon\" to \"extension host\" throughout Library.rs, Host.rs, Server/mod.rs, and Client/mod.rs to reflect the architecture accurately — the Node.js runtime hosts extensions but is not itself named Cocoon in the formal component model. Update port descriptions in Library.rs accordingly. Replace repository-relative doc links with absolute GitHub URLs. Format doc comments with consistent em-dash section separators, parameter/return/error documentation blocks, and bulleted tables for enumerations.\n\nEach notification atom now carries a one-line doc comment matching its Cocoon method name and Sky event destination, making the dispatcher role clear at a glance. The Error module gains a full gRPC status-code mapping table and IsRecoverable variant enumeration. Shared.rs has every static, const, and function documented with purpose, lifecycle, and parameters.\n\nNo behavioral changes — purely documentation and reference consistency.",
			"SHA": "5a249d621523f42354f1379ecfefc285f88a60cf"
		},
