				2515,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add cancellable unary requests with CancelOperation\n\nIntroduce `FnCancellable` in `SendRequest` alongside the existing `Fn` entry point. The new function accepts a `watch::Receiver<bool>` cancel signal; when the caller flips it mid-flight a best-effort `CancelOperation` gRPC request carrying the wire `RequestIdentifier` is sent to the sidecar, and `VineError::RequestCanceled` is returned. The original `Fn` delegates to `FnCancellable` with a process-lifetime `NeverCancelled()` signal via `OnceLock`, preserving backward compatibility for existing callers.\n\nA unary timeout now also fires a best-effort `CancelOperation` so the sidecar can abort work Mountain has already stopped waiting for.\n\nAdd comprehensive doc comments across every module: `Client` (NotificationFrame, SendRequest, Shared, mod), `Error` (variant table, recoverability, `tonic::Status` mapping), `Host`, `Library`, `Multiplexer`, and all `Server` notification atoms. Normalise references from \"Cocoon\" to \"extension host\" throughout to reflect the architecture accurately. Format doc comments with consistent em-dash section separators.\n\nCallers of `SendRequest::Fn` see no change. Callers that want cancellation support can switch to `FnCancellable` and provide a `watch::Receiver<bool>`.",
			"SHA": "b37bfedb2b7149f3a8213ce2a5010c8e64bac7f7"
		},
		{
